Copyright: work of the ORDunwoody subproject (node N13 of the
`annals_on_coherence_of_one_relator_groups` project).

# (W2) again, on an import path free of `Dunwoody/ArcPrefStep.lean`

`Dunwoody/RegionAlpha.lean` proves (W2) — the counting side function `sideV τ` of a track is
constant on the classes of `RegionRel`, so that it descends to `sideOfRegion τ : Region D → ZMod 2`
— but it imports both `Dunwoody/AlphaSide.lean` and (transitively, through
`midSum_chord.lean → midSum_Ico.lean`) `Dunwoody/ArcPrefStep.lean`, and those two files both
declare `Work.ORDunwoody.Dunwoody.midSum_cons`; a module importing both does not build.

This file reproves the same statements on an import path that avoids `ArcPrefStep.lean` entirely,
under `res`-prefixed names, so that the assembly of the dual tree
(`Dunwoody/ResolutionAssembly.lean`) has a route that does not depend on the resolution of that
clash.  Nothing here is new mathematics; it is the same argument as `RegionAlpha.lean`, with the
few inputs that live in the conflicting files (`midSum_Ico`, `isChord_irrefl`, `chord_midInd`,
`midSum_chord_aux`) proved here.

The content is:

* `resMidSum_Ico` and `resMidSum_chord_aux`: for a chord `(p, q)` of a nested matching with unique
  partners and no self-chords, the track indicator sums over the closed and open intervals
  `[p, q]`, `(p, q)` vanish;
* `resMidSum_eq_of_pieceRel`: the sum `midSum τ vs i` depends only on the *piece* of the arc index
  `i` (the equivalence relation generated by the chords);
* `resSideV_eq_of_regionRel` and the descent `resSideOfRegion`, with the two wall-system axioms
  `resSideOfRegion_ne_of_inc`, `resSideOfRegion_eq_of_inc_of_ne`.
-/
